+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
+<!-- One short imperative label per registered command.
+
+`docs/COMMAND_PALETTE_CONTRACT.md` section 5(1): every command in
+`first_party/commands.json` needs a localised user-facing title, and it belongs
+in Chromium's localisation system rather than in a WebUI bundle, because the
+toolbar, the menus and the gestures invoke commands too and none of them can
+read a bundle. `summary` in the registry is a developer-facing sentence ending
+in a period; this is the row a person reads.
+
+The message name is derived from the command identifier the same way the
+telemetry name is -- `browser.zoom.in` becomes IDS_SUNSHINE_COMMAND_BROWSER_ZOOM_IN
+-- so the two cannot drift apart by being typed separately.
+`scripts/validate_commands.py` fails when a registered command has no message
+here, and when a message here names no registered command.
+
+The outputs below mirror `chrome/app/chromium_strings.grd`, one locale at a
+time, because that file is one this build already produces and copying a
+working list is the only way to be right about it without a compiler. A guard
+holds the two in step, so a Chromium roll that adds a locale fails a check
+rather than a six-hour build.
+
+There is no <translations> block. No .xtb exists for any of these strings and
+this project has no translation pipeline, so every locale carries the source
+text. That is what Chromium does for any new string until translation lands,
+and it is stated here rather than left to be discovered. -->
+
